{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792951394,"nonce":"seAIiAjRbPPqgMjeWgpprcltcqQ=","title":"Keep browser frames in one GPU batch","message":"The real Chrome RayDE page shows Welcome, then becomes blank after input. GPU validation reports a destroyed swapchain texture used in submit. Probe of the xgpu agent shows every acquired frame sent separately from its render/submit batch (getCurrentTexture + createView, then the draw). RayDE GpuProgress.attach installs device.poll in LayoutTree.flushHooks to reclaim completed native work; Offscreen.render flushes the tree after acquiring a surface, so that hook flushes the browser mailbox in the middle of the frame. Do not attach this native-only maintenance hook for WASM; presentation and error checks already flush the browser commands. Verify zero cross-batch submissions, GPU errors, opening and typing in Main.hx, and visible pixels.\n\nAlso probe readiness and memory at the GPU boundary: shared WASM capacity versus live GC blocks versus logical texture/buffer bytes and browser RSS; completion of first submitted work versus ashui ready; worker-pool cost. Related browser run issue 87a3c309b1fc6f24e8380f66ff8250c43e67016db2a09dcf2022e021bf435ad0 and fonts issue 3fb726bd42e7fb43a3d10c0144dfc09c81646a6280f0a56e67599ba4583c7699.","files":null}]}